32:["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"Nasal blockage is a common symptom of sinusitis. Inflammation and swelling of the nasal and sinus lining can reduce airflow and interfere with normal sinus drainage. However, not every case of nasal blockage is caused by sinusitis."}]
33:["$","details","Can nasal blockage affect sleep?",{"className":"group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-slate-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"Can nasal blockage affect sleep?"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-teal-50 text-xl text-teal-700 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"Yes. Difficulty breathing through the nose can contribute to mouth breathing, snoring and disturbed sleep. Persistent nighttime nasal obstruction should be evaluated, particularly when it is associated with loud snoring, pauses in breathing or excessive daytime tiredness."}]]}]
34:["$","details","When should I see an ENT doctor for nasal blockage?",{"className":"group rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 shadow-sm","children":[["$","summary",null,{"className":"flex cursor-pointer list-none items-center justify-between gap-4 font-semibold text-slate-900","children":[["$","span",null,{"children":"When should I see an ENT doctor for nasal blockage?"}],["$","span",null,{"className":"flex h-8 w-8 shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-teal-50 text-xl text-teal-700 transition-transform duration-300 group-open:rotate-45","children":"+"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-4 border-t border-slate-100 pt-4 text-sm leading-7 text-slate-600","children":"You should consider an ENT consultation if nasal blockage persists, repeatedly returns, affects sleep or exercise, is mainly present on one side, causes recurrent sinus symptoms, or is associated with nosebleeds, reduced smell or facial pressure."}]]}]
